Specialized skill for testing file system operations using
System.IO.Abstractions. Use when you need to test File, Directory, Path
operations, or simulate file system. Covers IFileSystem, MockFileSystem, file
read/write testing, directory operation testing, etc.
System.IO.Abstractions-based tests can verify file contents, file existence, directory creation, line counts, file metadata, copy behavior, and timestamped backups without using disk state.

Current State:
**Core Interface Architecture**:
public interface IFileSystem
IFile File { get; }
IDirectory Directory { get; }
IFileInfo FileInfo { get; }
IDirectoryInfo DirectoryInfo { get; }
IPath Path { get; }
IDriveInfo DriveInfo { get; }
System.IO.Abstractions wraps System.IO static classes behind interfaces and supports dependency injection and test doubles.

Preferences:
Keep filesystem tests focused by creating only files necessary for the test and avoiding oversized simulated files; use moderately sized data for large-file logic.

